Simplest rigorous approach: define
```
def Torus (n : ℕ) := (Fin n → ℝ) ⧸ ((Fin n → ℤ) →+ (Fin n → ℝ))
```
where the map is the coercion homomorphism. But defining group quotients with `QuotientAddGroup` works: `QuotientAddGroup.quotient` of any additive subgroup. `(Fin n → ℤ)` is an additive subgroup of `(Fin n → ℝ)` via the coercion map... but it's not literally a subgroup; the image is. We could use `AddSubgroup.map`? There's `Subgroup.map`. Alternatively define the subgroup as `{x | ∀ i, x i ∈ range ...}`. Simpler: define a map `intVec : (Fin n → ℤ) →+ (Fin n → ℝ)` and then the subgroup is its range: `intVec.range` — `AddMonoidHom.range`. Then `Torus n := (Fin n → ℝ) ⧸ intVecHom.range`.

