/-!
# D11 — Spectral theory of the flat torus: basic objects

The flat n-torus as ℝⁿ/ℤⁿ, the Fourier modes `e_k` indexed by `k : ℤⁿ`, and the bridge to
mathlib's `UnitAddTorus` (the product of unit circles), which carries the L² theory
(`orthonormal_mFourier`) used for Parseval's identity.
